name va-shadow-implicit
# A verb synset (BabelNet's key of it, read as the ILI concept), a role of its frame, and the synsets that fill the
# role as a shadow argument (VA_bn2shadow) or an implicit one (VA_bn2implicit), as the file's name says after its "2":
# the row says together that the synset has the role as such an argument, and what fills it. The fillers are written
# with | between them. The first line is the release's banner, not a row.
match VA_bn2shadow.tsv VA_bn2implicit.tsv

tier row by \n
skip 1
names synset role filler
tier field by \t
part filler by |

stem 2 .
thing row synset
type synset ili
# A filler is a BabelNet synset, nearly always a noun's (bn:00030466n): VerbAtlas's bn2wn maps only verbs to WordNet,
# so a filler read as the ILI concept resolved to nothing and its claim was never made. It is recorded as written, as
# VA_preference_info's reference synsets are.
content role filler
together row
relate row {file} to role
# a role is a value of VerbAtlas's role inventory (Agent, Theme, ...), the relation of the frame to its filler. The
# file's name (shadow, implicit) is no relation: an unresolved obligation (relate {file}). The README: "6.
# VA_bn2shadow.tsv Each line contains the shadow arguments, if any, for each BabelNet synset ID." and "7.
# VA_bn2implicit.tsv Each line contains the implicit arguments": that an argument is shadow or implicit is written only
# in the file's name, and the recipe language cannot yet say a file's name as a value of the argument (value refuses
# {file}): it stays an obligation until it can (Laplace-Engine#32).
value - role
relate row role to filler
